Q: How to prevent anchor with query string from reloading page A: <p>I had the same problem and finally solved it with a JavaScript approach mentioned in other posts (<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/10970078/modifying-a-query-string-without-reloading-the-page">Modifying a query string without reloading the page</a> and <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/824349/how-do-i-modify-the-url-without-reloading-the-page">How do I modify the URL without reloading the page?</a>).</p>
<p>HTML/PHP:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>
&lt;h1&gt;In-Home Chef&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;a id=&quot;in-home-chef&quot; href=&quot;#explore&quot;&gt;
  Experience the luxury of your very own in-home chef!
&lt;/a&gt;


&lt;!-- Explore Experiences --&gt;
&lt;section id=&quot;explore&quot;&gt;...&lt;/section&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Your example was missing a <code>key</code> for your <code>value</code> of &quot;in-home-chef-experiences&quot;.  This example uses the key, <code>choice</code>.</p>
<p>JavaScript:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const url = new URL(document.URL);

// --&gt; url is now https://iamhoste.com/experiences

if (url) {
    // Prepare your new url with the desired modifications
    url.searchParams.set('choice', 'in home chef experiences');

    // --&gt; url is now https://iamhoste.com/experiences/?choice=in+home+chef+experiences#explore

    // Update the url on the page
    if (window.history.pushState) {
        window.history.pushState(null, '', url);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/History/pushState" rel="nofollow noreferrer">pushState</a> will give you that &quot;Wikipedia&quot; feel -- clicking links jumps you down the page; clicking the Back button takes you back to the previous link on the same page.</p>
<p>If you don't want to retrace every in-page anchor you've visited, use <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/History/replaceState" rel="nofollow noreferrer">replaceState</a> instead.  It's tantamount to clicking links to jump all around a Wikipedia page, pressing the Back button, and instead of going back to the previous anchor/hash, you go directly back to the previous page.</p>

Q: Using &quot;this-&gt;member_variable&quot; as template function parameter A: <p>You can make LOG a member function and use CRTP</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;class X&gt;
struct LOGGER {
  template&lt;class ... Whatever&gt;
  auto LOG (Whatever ...) -&gt; void {
     static_cast&lt;X*&gt;(this)-&gt;m_member; 
  }
};

class Faewe : public LOGGER&lt;Faewe&gt; {
    public:
        int m_member {73};
        auto doSomething() -&gt; void { 
          LOG(&quot;hello&quot;);
        }      
};


</code></pre>

Q: After set body display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; , the web page is cut off on the top. Why? A: <p>After read some resource, I add two CSS properties:</p>
<pre><code>flex-direction:column;
min-height:100vh;
</code></pre>
<p>solved this problem.</p>

Q: Convert Number to Words for Kuwait Dinar A: <ol>
<li><p>Press Alt + F11 keys to open the Microsoft Visual Basic for Application window.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Click Insert &gt; Module and paste below VBA to the new Module window.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<pre><code>Function SpellKD(ByVal MyNumber)

 '**** Created by Ariful Islam
 '**** arifulsh.com
 '**** Last updated 02-April-2021
 '**** SpellKD shows KD to precede, and to show &quot;&quot; for 0 Fils)
 '****************' Main Function *'****************

Dim Kuwaiti_Dinar, Fils, Temp
Dim DecimalPlace, Count
ReDim Place(9) As String
Place(2) = &quot; Thousand &quot;
Place(3) = &quot; Lac &quot;
Place(4) = &quot; Crore &quot;
Place(5) = &quot; Arab &quot; ' String representation of amount
MyNumber = Trim(Str(MyNumber)) ' Position of decimal place 0 if none
DecimalPlace = InStr(MyNumber, &quot;.&quot;)
 ' Convert Fils and set MyNumber to Dinar amount
If DecimalPlace &gt; 0 Then
    Fils = GetTens(Left(Mid(MyNumber, DecimalPlace + 1) &amp; &quot;00&quot;, 2))
    MyNumber = Trim(Left(MyNumber, DecimalPlace - 1))
End If
Count = 1
Do While MyNumber &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot;
    If Count = 1 Then Temp = GetHundreds(Right(MyNumber, 3))
    If Count &gt; 1 Then Temp = GetHundreds(Right(MyNumber, 2))
    If Temp &lt;&gt; &quot;&quot; Then Kuwaiti_Dinar = Temp &amp; Place(Count) &amp; Kuwaiti_Dinar
    If Count = 1 And Len(MyNumber) &gt; 3 Then
        MyNumber = Left(MyNumber, Len(MyNumber) - 3)
    Else
        If Count &gt; 1 And Len(MyNumber) &gt; 2 Then
            MyNumber = Left(MyNumber, Len(MyNumber) - 2)
        Else
            MyNumber = &quot;&quot;
        End If
    End If
    Count = Count + 1
 Loop
Select Case Kuwaiti_Dinar
Case &quot;&quot;
    KD = &quot;&quot;
Case &quot;One&quot;
    KD = &quot;One Kuwaiti Dinar&quot;
Case Else
     '****************************************************************
     'modified the following two lines to display &quot;KD&quot; to precede
     ' rem'd the first line and added the second line
     '****************************************************************
     'KD = KD &amp; &quot; KD&quot;
    Kuwaiti_Dinar = Kuwaiti_Dinar &amp; &quot; Kuwaiti Dinnar&quot;

End Select
Select Case Fils
Case &quot;&quot;
     '****************************************************************
     'modified the following two lines to display nothing for no Fils
     ' rem'd the first line and added the second line
     '****************************************************************

     'Fils = &quot; and No Fils&quot;
     '****************************************************************
     'modified the following line to display &quot; Only&quot; for no Fils
     ' rem'd the first line and added the second line
     '****************************************************************
     'Fils = &quot;&quot;
    Fils = &quot; Only&quot;
Case &quot;One&quot;
    Fils = &quot; and One Fils&quot;
Case Else
    Fils = &quot; and &quot; &amp; Fils &amp; &quot;Fils&quot;

End Select
SpellKD = Kuwaiti_Dinar &amp; Fils
End Function

'*******************************************
' Converts a number from 100-999 into text *
'*******************************************
Function GetHundreds(ByVal MyNumber)
Dim Result As String
If Val(MyNumber) = 0 Then Exit Function
MyNumber = Right(&quot;000&quot; &amp; MyNumber, 3) 'Convert the hundreds place
If Mid(MyNumber, 1, 1) &lt;&gt; &quot;0&quot; Then
    Result = GetDigit(Mid(MyNumber, 1, 1)) &amp; &quot; Hundred &quot;
End If
 'Convert the tens and ones place
If Mid(MyNumber, 2, 1) &lt;&gt; &quot;0&quot; Then
    Result = Result &amp; GetTens(Mid(MyNumber, 2))
Else
    Result = Result &amp; GetDigit(Mid(MyNumber, 3))
End If
GetHundreds = Result
End Function
'*********************************************
' Converts a number from 10 to 99 into text. *
'*********************************************
Function GetTens(TensText)
Dim Result As String
Result = &quot;&quot; ' null out the temporary function value

If Val(Left(TensText, 1)) = 1 Then ' If value between 10-19
    Select Case Val(TensText)
    Case 10: Result = &quot;Ten&quot;
    Case 11: Result = &quot;Eleven&quot;
    Case 12: Result = &quot;Twelve&quot;
    Case 13: Result = &quot;Thirteen&quot;
    Case 14: Result = &quot;Fourteen&quot;
    Case 15: Result = &quot;Fifteen&quot;
    Case 16: Result = &quot;Sixteen&quot;
    Case 17: Result = &quot;Seventeen&quot;
    Case 18: Result = &quot;Eighteen&quot;
    Case 19: Result = &quot;Nineteen&quot;
    Case Else
    End Select
Else ' If value between 20-99
    Select Case Val(Left(TensText, 1))
    Case 2: Result = &quot;Twenty &quot;
    Case 3: Result = &quot;Thirty &quot;
    Case 4: Result = &quot;Forty &quot;
    Case 5: Result = &quot;Fifty &quot;
    Case 6: Result = &quot;Sixty &quot;
    Case 7: Result = &quot;Seventy &quot;
    Case 8: Result = &quot;Eighty &quot;
    Case 9: Result = &quot;Ninety &quot;
    Case Else
    End Select
    Result = Result &amp; GetDigit _
    (Right(TensText, 1)) 'Retrieve ones place
End If
GetTens = Result
End Function
'*******************************************
' Converts a number from 1 to 9 into text. *
'*******************************************
Function GetDigit(Digit)
Select Case Val(Digit)
Case 1: GetDigit = &quot;One&quot;
Case 2: GetDigit = &quot;Two&quot;
Case 3: GetDigit = &quot;Three&quot;
Case 4: GetDigit = &quot;Four&quot;
Case 5: GetDigit = &quot;Five&quot;
Case 6: GetDigit = &quot;Six&quot;
Case 7: GetDigit = &quot;Seven&quot;
Case 8: GetDigit = &quot;Eight&quot;
Case 9: GetDigit = &quot;Nine&quot;
Case Else: GetDigit = &quot;&quot;
End Select
End Function
</code></pre>
<p>But it will never work on more then 99 fils. It will count only first 2 number of fils.</p>
